{"content_hash": "cf9f343b16c22dca", "version_id": 684, "article_id": 69, "level_code": "en_b2", "lang": "en", "level": 4, "level_label": "B2 中高级", "title": "Father fined €3,000 after son, 2, died in Cyprus hotel fall", "title_zh": "两岁儿子在塞浦路斯酒店坠亡，父亲被罚3000欧元", "has_translation": true, "topic": "world", "source": "bbc_world", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cvj6j1klez88o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1437943085269-6da5dd4295bf?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8MTB8fGRhZCUyMGZpbmVkJTIwc29ufGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTIxOTQ0ODR8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Steven Van Loy on Unsplash", "author": "Steven Van Loy", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@mafalou?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/man-wears-blue-crew-neck-t-shirt-holding-toddler-wears-black-hooded-jacket-near-ocean-under-blue-sky-at-daytime-oUhSla4L_98?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(165, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(203, 46%, 48%)", "label": "WORLD", "seed": "f11dca163925"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-17", "word_count": 235, "reading_minutes": 1.2, "lead": "A British father has been fined €3,000 after his two-year-old son fell to his death from a hotel window in Cyprus. The court heard that the window appeared to be closed when he placed the boy on the sill.", "lead_zh": "一位英国父亲因两岁儿子从塞浦路斯酒店窗户坠亡而被罚款3000欧元。法庭获悉，他把孩子放在窗台上时，窗户看上去是关着的。", "preview": "Joshua Foster, 37, from Essex, admitted causing his son's death through a reckless, rash or dangerous act. The toddler fell nearly 40ft (12.", "preview_zh": "来自埃塞克斯的37岁男子乔舒亚·福斯特承认，他因鲁莽、轻率或危险的行为导致儿子死亡。7月12日，这家人在克洛拉卡斯度假的第一天，这名幼儿从五星级的国王埃维尔顿海滩酒店及度假村四楼窗户坠落，高度近40英尺（12.1米）。帕福斯地区法院对福斯特处以3000欧元（2500英镑）罚款。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 674, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/69/en_b2.mp3", "duration": 81.525, "size_bytes": 490176, "engine": "kokoro", "voice": "af_heart", "word_count": 271, "has_timeline": true, "alternates": [{"voice": "af_bella", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/69/en_b2_af_bella.mp3", "duration": 83.075, "size_bytes": 499392, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 271, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/69/en_b2_af_bella.json"}, {"voice": "am_michael", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/69/en_b2_am_michael.mp3", "duration": 89.15, "size_bytes": 535824, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 271, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/69/en_b2_am_michael.json"}, {"voice": "bf_emma", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/69/en_b2_bf_emma.mp3", "duration": 76.95, "size_bytes": 462672, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 271, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/69/en_b2_bf_emma.json"}, {"voice": "bm_george", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/69/en_b2_bm_george.mp3", "duration": 81.8, "size_bytes": 491760, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 271, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/69/en_b2_bm_george.json"}]}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@0da0f65/content/data/versions/684.json", "paragraphs": ["Joshua Foster, 37, from Essex, admitted causing his son's death through a reckless, rash or dangerous act. The toddler fell nearly 40ft (12.1m) from a fourth-floor window at the five-star King Evelthon Beach Hotel and Resort on 12 July, the first day of the family's holiday in Chlorakas. Foster was fined €3,000 (£2,500) by Paphos District Court.", "The court heard that Foster thought the window was closed when he placed his son on the sill to show him the view of a waterpark. He then \"lost control\" of the child. The boy was taken to Paphos General Hospital, where he was later pronounced dead. In a voluntary statement to police, Foster said the boy \"fell before he had a chance to grab him\".", "District Judge Froso Christodoulidou said the window did not appear to have markings that would have alerted Foster to the fact that one section was open. She described the incident as a momentary error with fatal consequences, and added that there was no evidence he had deliberately exposed the child to danger.", "After the sentencing, Foster told reporters he was looking forward to going home to his wife and daughter. His lawyer, Alexandros Alexandrou, argued that the case should never have gone to court, saying Foster had lost the chance to grieve with his family. The family said in a statement that their son was deeply loved and would be forever missed."], "paragraphs_zh": ["来自埃塞克斯的37岁男子乔舒亚·福斯特承认，他因鲁莽、轻率或危险的行为导致儿子死亡。7月12日，这家人在克洛拉卡斯度假的第一天，这名幼儿从五星级的国王埃维尔顿海滩酒店及度假村四楼窗户坠落，高度近40英尺（12.1米）。帕福斯地区法院对福斯特处以3000欧元（2500英镑）罚款。", "法庭获悉，福斯特把儿子放在窗台上看水上乐园时，以为窗户是关着的。随后他“失手”没抓住孩子。男孩被送往帕福斯综合医院，随后被宣告死亡。在自愿向警方提供的陈述中，福斯特说，孩子“在他来得及抓住之前就掉了下去”。", "地区法官弗罗索·赫里斯托祖利杜表示，窗户上似乎没有标记能让福斯特意识到其中一扇是开着的。她称这起事件是一个带来致命后果的瞬间失误，并补充说，没有证据表明他故意让孩子处于危险之中。", "宣判后，福斯特告诉记者，他期待回家与妻子和女儿团聚。他的律师亚历山德罗斯·亚历山德鲁认为，此案根本不该上法庭，并称福斯特失去了与家人一起哀悼的机会。这家人在一份声明中表示，他们的儿子深受疼爱，将永远被怀念。"], "body": "Joshua Foster, 37, from Essex, admitted causing his son's death through a reckless, rash or dangerous act. The toddler fell nearly 40ft (12.1m) from a fourth-floor window at the five-star King Evelthon Beach Hotel and Resort on 12 July, the first day of the family's holiday in Chlorakas. Foster was fined €3,000 (£2,500) by Paphos District Court.\n\nThe court heard that Foster thought the window was closed when he placed his son on the sill to show him the view of a waterpark. He then \"lost control\" of the child. The boy was taken to Paphos General Hospital, where he was later pronounced dead. In a voluntary statement to police, Foster said the boy \"fell before he had a chance to grab him\".\n\nDistrict Judge Froso Christodoulidou said the window did not appear to have markings that would have alerted Foster to the fact that one section was open. She described the incident as a momentary error with fatal consequences, and added that there was no evidence he had deliberately exposed the child to danger.\n\nAfter the sentencing, Foster told reporters he was looking forward to going home to his wife and daughter. His lawyer, Alexandros Alexandrou, argued that the case should never have gone to court, saying Foster had lost the chance to grieve with his family. The family said in a statement that their son was deeply loved and would be forever missed.", "body_zh": "来自埃塞克斯的37岁男子乔舒亚·福斯特承认，他因鲁莽、轻率或危险的行为导致儿子死亡。7月12日，这家人在克洛拉卡斯度假的第一天，这名幼儿从五星级的国王埃维尔顿海滩酒店及度假村四楼窗户坠落，高度近40英尺（12.1米）。帕福斯地区法院对福斯特处以3000欧元（2500英镑）罚款。\n\n法庭获悉，福斯特把儿子放在窗台上看水上乐园时，以为窗户是关着的。随后他“失手”没抓住孩子。男孩被送往帕福斯综合医院，随后被宣告死亡。在自愿向警方提供的陈述中，福斯特说，孩子“在他来得及抓住之前就掉了下去”。\n\n地区法官弗罗索·赫里斯托祖利杜表示，窗户上似乎没有标记能让福斯特意识到其中一扇是开着的。她称这起事件是一个带来致命后果的瞬间失误，并补充说，没有证据表明他故意让孩子处于危险之中。\n\n宣判后，福斯特告诉记者，他期待回家与妻子和女儿团聚。他的律师亚历山德罗斯·亚历山德鲁认为，此案根本不该上法庭，并称福斯特失去了与家人一起哀悼的机会。这家人在一份声明中表示，他们的儿子深受疼爱，将永远被怀念。", "text": "Joshua Foster, 37, from Essex, admitted causing his son's death through a reckless, rash or dangerous act. The toddler fell nearly 40ft (12.1m) from a fourth-floor window at the five-star King Evelthon Beach Hotel and Resort on 12 July, the first day of the family's holiday in Chlorakas. Foster was fined €3,000 (£2,500) by Paphos District Court. The court heard that Foster thought the window was closed when he placed his son on the sill to show him the view of a waterpark. He then \"lost control\" of the child. The boy was taken to Paphos General Hospital, where he was later pronounced dead. In a voluntary statement to police, Foster said the boy \"fell before he had a chance to grab him\". District Judge Froso Christodoulidou said the window did not appear to have markings that would have alerted Foster to the fact that one section was open. She described the incident as a momentary error with fatal consequences, and added that there was no evidence he had deliberately exposed the child to danger. After the sentencing, Foster told reporters he was looking forward to going home to his wife and daughter. His lawyer, Alexandros Alexandrou, argued that the case should never have gone to court, saying Foster had lost the chance to grieve with his family. The family said in a statement that their son was deeply loved and would be forever missed.", "vocab": [{"word": "admit", "pos": "verb", "zh": "承认", "note": "admit doing sth 或 admit that...", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "reckless", "pos": "adj", "zh": "鲁莽的，不计后果的", "note": "常与 act、behaviour 搭配", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "toddler", "pos": "noun", "zh": "幼儿，学步儿童", "note": "一般指1至3岁的小孩", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "sill", "pos": "noun", "zh": "窗台", "note": "window sill 的简称", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "pronounce dead", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "宣告死亡", "note": "常用于医院或官方场合", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "voluntary statement", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "自愿陈述", "note": "法律语境中指主动向警方提供的证词", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "alert", "pos": "verb", "zh": "使警觉，提醒", "note": "alert sb to sth 表示使某人意识到某事", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "momentary", "pos": "adj", "zh": "瞬间的，短暂的", "note": "强调时间极短", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "fatal", "pos": "adj", "zh": "致命的", "note": "fatal consequences 致命后果", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "deliberately", "pos": "adv", "zh": "故意地", "note": "反义词是 accidentally", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "grieve", "pos": "verb", "zh": "悲伤，哀悼", "note": "名词形式为 grief", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "custody", "pos": "noun", "zh": "拘留，监护", "note": "in custody 表示被拘留", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "Dad fined after son, 2, died in Cyprus hotel fall", "summary_original": "Joshua Foster \"lost control\" of his son while showing him the view of a water park from a window.", "body_original": "Dad fined after son, 2, died in Cyprus hotel fall\nBy\nLewis Adams\nEssex\nPublished\n16 October 2026, 10:31 BST\nUpdated 9 hours ago\nA father whose two-year-old boy fell from a fourth floor window of a Cyprus hotel has been fined €3,000 (£2,500) for causing his death.\nJoshua Foster thought the window was closed when he placed his son on a sill to show him the view of a waterpark\nand \"lost control\" of him\n, Paphos District Court previously heard.\nThe toddler fell nearly 40ft (12.1m) at the five-star King Evelthon Beach Hotel and Resort on 12 July, the first day of the family's holiday in Chlorakas.\nFoster, 37, from Essex, admitted causing death through a reckless, rash or dangerous act and was sentenced earlier.\nHe told reporters afterwards: \"Thank you for the support. I'm looking forward to going home and being with my wife and daughter.\"\nLater, the family said in a statement: \"We are relieved that this process is now over, but for our family, the consequences of this tragedy will never end.\n\"Our son was deeply loved and will be forever missed. His loss is something we carry with us every day.\"\nFoster, an auditor, arrived in Cyprus hours before the incident with his wife, two children and in-laws.\nThey enjoyed various activities and swimming, before getting ready for dinner in the evening.\nAt about 18:00, Foster, his father-in-law and son were walking towards a lift when the boy noticed a waterpark outside.\nFoster pushed the lift button, placed the child on the windowsill and the \"inconceivable\" unfolded before he could react, the court heard.\nThe boy was taken to Paphos General Hospital and later pronounced dead.\n\"The window did not appear to carry markings that would necessarily have alerted the defendant to the fact that one section was open,\" said District Judge Froso Christodoulidou.\nHis failure to establish that the window was not closed led to the tragic result, the judge added.\n\"It was a momentary error which created a dangerous situation with fatal consequences,\" he said.\nThe judge added there was \"no evidence that the defendant deliberately exposed the child to danger\", according to a translation of proceedings.\nShe added no sentence could outweigh the \"personal consequences of the loss of his child\".\nIn a voluntary statement to police, Foster said when he placed his son on the windowsill, the boy \"fell before he had a chance to grab him\".\nWhile Foster had alcohol in his system, it did not form a significant part of the case against him and his lawyer Alexandros Alexandrou said there was no testimony he was drunk.\nAfter the sentencing, Foster's lawyer, Alexandros Alexandrou, told reporters the case should have \"never gone to court\".\nHe said Foster was held in custody for eight days immediately after the incident and he had to call his daughter from custody to explain what had happened.\n\"Within this three months, there was a lost opportunity for this man to grieve as he wanted to, to be with his family,\" he said.\nHe described his client as an \"incredible father\".\n\"[He is] an exemplary family man with a beautiful family behind him, that support him, that embraces him, that has always been by his side.\"\nDo you have a story suggestion for Essex? Contact us below.\nGet in touch\nYour Voice\nContact form\nContact form\nFollow Essex news on\nBBC Sounds\n,\nFacebook\n,\nexternal\n,\nInstagram\n,\nexternal\nand\nX\n,\nexternal\n.\nRelated topics\nEssex\nPaphos\nCyprus\nMore on this story\nDad sees son fall to death from Cyprus hotel window\nPublished\n6 October\nFather admits causing death of his son in hotel fall\nPublished\n22 September\nRelated internet links\nHM Courts & Tribunals Service", "fetched_at": "2026-10-16T23:48:02.449828", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "Joshua", "s": 0.325, "e": 0.75, "sm": 325, "em": 750, "cs": 0, "ce": 6, "